From 0cad9f917b8997d3298238ef34bca42d318b0d48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:30:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MFront: rotation functions, method calls and slip systems
 usable on GPUs

- `BehaviourRotationFunctions`: description of the rotation functions of
  orthotropic behaviours and code rotating the values of one point with
  `change_basis`, shared by the `generic` and `generic-parallel`
  interfaces. Fixes of the `generic` interface: offset of the point of the
  second order tensors which are not the first variable in the array
  variants, scalars not copied, vectors and vector blocks not supported;
- the drivers of the `generic` interface call initialize functions and
  post-processings through function objects (`MethodCaller` keeps the
  pointer to member API on the host): calls through pointers to members
  are silently ignored by nvc++ in device code;
- `execute<Name>InitializeFunction` and `execute<Name>PostProcessing` are
  `TFEL_HOST_DEVICE`;
- the slip systems classes are built at compile time and accessed through
  `getConstantObject`, their methods are `TFEL_HOST_DEVICE`;
- `writeGenericBehaviourTraits` extracted from the generic interface.
---
